Question	Answer
What is file handling?	Performing operations on files to store and retrieve data.
Which header supports file handling in C++?	fstream
What is ifstream?	Input file stream used for reading files.
What is ofstream?	Output file stream used for writing files.
What is fstream?	A file stream supporting both reading and writing.
What is ios::app?	Opens a file in append mode.
What is ios::trunc?	Discards existing file contents when opening the file.
What is ios::binary?	Opens a file in binary mode.
What is getline()?	Reads a line of text.
How do you rename a file?	Using rename().
How do you delete a file?	Using remove().
What is EOF?	End of File.
What is secondary storage?	Non-volatile storage such as SSDs and hard disks.
Why should files be closed?	To release resources and ensure buffered output is flushed.
What is the difference between write and append?	Ordinary output mode can overwrite existing data, whereas append adds data at the end.
